1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,413
Terror From Beyond: there's no Killer. Alien Podarchs start as plants, grow into

2
00:00:04,413 --> 00:00:06,572
pods, and take over the people they catch.

3
00:00:06,792 --> 00:00:09,096
Here's how the vignette plays, at any Location.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:14,393
Setup in brief. There's no Killer board: line up the two Bloodlust cards beside the

5
00:00:14,393 --> 00:00:16,666
Location board, marker on the start space.

6
00:00:16,666 --> 00:00:17,857
Horror starts at four.

7
00:00:18,077 --> 00:00:22,038
Take every Event card showing Special Victim meeples out of the Event deck.

8
00:00:22,038 --> 00:00:26,315
Put an Assimilated token on a Victim meeple and place it in the Killer's starting

9
00:00:26,315 --> 00:00:26,632
space.

10
00:00:26,852 --> 00:00:31,158
Put the Reference card out Docile side up and the two Persuade cards in the Tableau.

11
00:00:31,158 --> 00:00:35,464
Put the Podarchs card above the Finale with the Podarch tokens, and place one, Plant

12
00:00:35,464 --> 00:00:37,668
side up, with the Victim furthest from you.

13
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:42,705
Podarchs exist in three states. A Plant, which grows into a Pod, which turns a

14
00:00:42,705 --> 00:00:44,537
Victim into an Assimilated person.

15
00:00:44,757 --> 00:00:48,533
There's no Killer meeple in this game. Your enemy is the whole infestation.

16
00:00:49,367 --> 00:00:52,247
Each Podarch token has a Plant side and a Pod side.

17
00:00:52,247 --> 00:00:55,127
A space can never hold more than one Podarch token.

18
00:00:55,347 --> 00:00:58,246
Plants and Pods count as Enemies, not Minions or a Killer.

19
00:00:58,246 --> 00:01:00,595
They have one health, and never move or attack.

20
00:01:00,815 --> 00:01:04,982
You can attack and destroy them: take the token off the board and back to the pool.

21
00:01:04,982 --> 00:01:07,492
Location effects that damage Enemies hit them too.

22
00:01:07,712 --> 00:01:12,131
When you attack a Plant or Pod, any leftover damage can go to an Assimilated in the

23
00:01:12,131 --> 00:01:14,048
same space, and the other way round.

24
00:01:14,867 --> 00:01:19,043
After the Planning phase and before the Killer phase there's a new Podarch Evolution

25
00:01:19,043 --> 00:01:20,584
phase. Do four steps, in order.

26
00:01:20,804 --> 00:01:24,924
One. If you're in a space with a Pod and there are no Victims in that space, you're

27
00:01:24,924 --> 00:01:28,399
assimilated and lose immediately. Don't check your Final Health token.

28
00:01:28,619 --> 00:01:32,407
Two. Remove every Plant and Pod in a space with neither you nor any Victims.

29
00:01:32,407 --> 00:01:33,653
They go back to the pool.

30
00:01:33,873 --> 00:01:36,924
Three. Each remaining Pod assimilates one Victim in its space.

31
00:01:37,144 --> 00:01:39,619
Four. Flip every remaining Plant to its Pod side.

32
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:44,409
A Plant sits with a lone Victim. At step four of Evolution it flips to a Pod.

33
00:01:44,409 --> 00:01:48,540
If the Victim is still there at the next Evolution, step three assimilates them.

34
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:52,471
So you have a full turn to act. Lead the Victim away, or destroy the Pod.

35
00:01:52,471 --> 00:01:56,589
If the Victim leaves and you're not there either, step two clears the token away.

36
00:01:56,809 --> 00:01:59,707
But never finish your turn alone in a space with a Pod.

37
00:01:59,707 --> 00:02:01,183
Step one is an instant loss.

38
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:06,176
When a Victim is assimilated, put an Assimilated token over the meeple's head.

39
00:02:06,176 --> 00:02:10,512
It's now an Assimilated person. Return the Pod token from that space to the pool.

40
00:02:10,732 --> 00:02:13,089
Once assimilated, they aren't Victims any more.

41
00:02:13,089 --> 00:02:15,596
Bloodlust doesn't rise, because no one was killed.

42
00:02:15,816 --> 00:02:20,145
If you ever need to assimilate a Victim but all twelve tokens are in use, you lose

43
00:02:20,145 --> 00:02:24,157
immediately. When an Assimilated is killed, its token goes back to the pool.

44
00:02:24,377 --> 00:02:26,861
Some effects say spawn an Assimilated in a space.

45
00:02:26,861 --> 00:02:29,903
Place a Victim meeple there with an Assimilated token on it.

46
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,586
The Podarchs take no joy in seeing Victims killed.

47
00:02:33,586 --> 00:02:35,811
Bloodlust only goes up for two reasons:

48
00:02:36,031 --> 00:02:40,041
when an Assimilated is killed, and when you see the green Podarch Bloodlust icon.

49
00:02:40,261 --> 00:02:44,635
Ignore every red Bloodlust icon, and don't raise Bloodlust when a Victim dies.

50
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:49,722
The Assimilated are Minions, using the Minion rules on page thirty two of the core

51
00:02:49,722 --> 00:02:53,874
rulebook. Each has one health. Their Movement and Attack values are shown on the

52
00:02:53,874 --> 00:02:54,704
Bloodlust track.

53
00:02:54,924 --> 00:02:59,076
Every Killer phase, all Assimilated perform the Minion Action on the back of the

54
00:02:59,076 --> 00:03:02,241
Finale card, one at a time, starting with the closest to you.

55
00:03:02,461 --> 00:03:06,827
Ones created in this turn's Evolution phase don't act in that first Minion Action.

56
00:03:06,827 --> 00:03:08,477
The Finale card has a reminder.

57
00:03:08,697 --> 00:03:12,797
When a Terror card or any other card gives a Killer Action, only the Assimilated

58
00:03:12,797 --> 00:03:14,180
closest to you performs it.

59
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,846
The Assimilated start the game Docile. Your meddling will eventually turn them

60
00:03:18,846 --> 00:03:19,437
against you.

61
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:23,659
When the Bloodlust marker reaches the start of the Hostile section of the track,

62
00:03:23,659 --> 00:03:27,060
they become Hostile. Flip the Reference card from Docile to Hostile.

63
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,947
How they move and attack depends on which side is showing.

64
00:03:30,767 --> 00:03:34,863
While Docile, you can't attack or kill the Assimilated, though Location effects that

65
00:03:34,863 --> 00:03:36,569
damage Enemies can still kill them.

66
00:03:36,789 --> 00:03:41,166
They follow normal targeting, except they ignore every target that already has a

67
00:03:41,166 --> 00:03:45,708
Podarch token in its space. If every possible target has one, they neither move nor

68
00:03:45,708 --> 00:03:46,091
attack.

69
00:03:46,311 --> 00:03:50,435
When they resolve an attack, if they're in the same space as you or a Victim, and

70
00:03:50,435 --> 00:03:53,541
there's no Podarch token there yet, they place a Plant token.

71
00:03:53,541 --> 00:03:54,865
Otherwise they do nothing.

72
00:03:55,700 --> 00:03:58,353
Ginny looks at the Minion Action on the Finale's back:

73
00:03:58,353 --> 00:04:00,564
choose the closest target, move, then attack.

74
00:04:00,784 --> 00:04:04,449
The Assimilated at the Hidden Lab goes first, as it's closest to her.

75
00:04:04,449 --> 00:04:08,646
The two nearest spaces with Ginny or Victims already have Podarch tokens, so it

76
00:04:08,646 --> 00:04:11,408
ignores them and moves towards a Victim without one.

77
00:04:11,628 --> 00:04:15,873
It only moves one space, ending with two Victims, but there's already a Podarch

78
00:04:15,873 --> 00:04:20,334
token there, so no Plant. The other Assimilated finds its nearest target taken too,

79
00:04:20,334 --> 00:04:22,913
so it heads south and plants with a lone Victim.

80
00:04:23,733 --> 00:04:27,881
Hostile Assimilated still treat Victims as before, placing Plants and trying to

81
00:04:27,881 --> 00:04:30,453
assimilate them. But now they just want you dead.

82
00:04:30,673 --> 00:04:34,663
When a Hostile one targets the closest Victim or Final Girl, or targets you

83
00:04:34,663 --> 00:04:38,866
directly, you're always a valid target, even if there's a Podarch token in your

84
00:04:38,866 --> 00:04:39,185
space.

85
00:04:39,405 --> 00:04:43,649
When an Assimilated in your space resolves an attack, it attacks you, dealing damage

86
00:04:43,649 --> 00:04:47,639
equal to the Attack value on the Bloodlust track, whatever it was targeting and

87
00:04:47,639 --> 00:04:49,155
whatever else is in the space.

88
00:04:49,375 --> 00:04:52,148
The good news: once they're Hostile, you can attack them too.

89
00:04:52,967 --> 00:04:55,390
Later, Bloodlust has reached the Hostile section.

90
00:04:55,390 --> 00:04:59,495
The Assimilated at the Airstrip would normally go for the Victim in the Hidden Lab.

91
00:04:59,715 --> 00:05:04,107
But Ginny is closer, and now she's always a valid target, even with a Podarch token

92
00:05:04,107 --> 00:05:07,864
in her space. It moves in and attacks her for its current Attack value.

93
00:05:08,084 --> 00:05:12,291
The other Assimilated targets the Victim at the Hidden Lab, moves, and places a

94
00:05:12,291 --> 00:05:15,700
Plant. Even Hostile, they convert Victims rather than kill them.

95
00:05:16,533 --> 00:05:20,183
Victims think your theories are crazy. They won't follow you, and can't be saved,

96
00:05:20,183 --> 00:05:22,571
until they've been persuaded that something is wrong.

97
00:05:22,791 --> 00:05:26,857
When you successfully resolve a Persuade Action card and a Victim is Persuaded,

98
00:05:26,857 --> 00:05:30,511
replace their yellow meeple with a Special Victim meeple of any colour.

99
00:05:30,511 --> 00:05:33,393
Persuaded Victims follow you and can be saved as normal.

100
00:05:33,613 --> 00:05:37,829
When a Persuaded Victim is killed, saved or assimilated, swap the Special Victim

101
00:05:37,829 --> 00:05:40,675
meeple back for a normal one, so it can be used again.

102
00:05:40,895 --> 00:05:44,824
If all the Special Victim meeples are in use, the rule sheet says you cannot play

103
00:05:44,824 --> 00:05:47,104
the... and the sentence is cut off on our copy.

104
00:05:47,104 --> 00:05:49,577
Presumably the Persuade card, but check your sheet.

105
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:53,905
Victims in a space with Assimilated don't panic in the Panic phase.

106
00:05:53,905 --> 00:05:55,840
Most don't believe anything is wrong.

107
00:05:56,060 --> 00:06:00,361
If an effect moves or places the Killer, or places something relative to the Killer,

108
00:06:00,361 --> 00:06:02,204
apply it to the closest Assimilated.

109
00:06:02,424 --> 00:06:06,933
Minor Dark Powers apply to all Assimilated, and can only be removed when you save a

110
00:06:06,933 --> 00:06:11,441
Victim. If a Location's Minor Dark Power has spaces for Health markers, don't place

111
00:06:11,441 --> 00:06:15,352
them; discard it when you save a Victim, or when the Finale is revealed.

112
00:06:15,572 --> 00:06:19,382
If an Event or Item card makes no sense here, ignore it or draw another.

113
00:06:19,382 --> 00:06:23,405
And if you need to place a Podarch token but they're all on the board, place

114
00:06:23,405 --> 00:06:23,828
nothing.

115
00:06:24,633 --> 00:06:28,561
The vignette has three Dark Power cards. Their effects are printed on the cards, not

116
00:06:28,561 --> 00:06:30,479
the rule sheet, so read the one you draw.

117
00:06:30,699 --> 00:06:34,540
The Finale reveals as normal, in the Upkeep after the Terror deck runs out.

118
00:06:34,540 --> 00:06:38,740
But if there are no Victims on the board at the end of a Killer phase, discard the

119
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:41,301
rest of the Terror deck, so the Finale comes next.

120
00:06:41,521 --> 00:06:45,839
When it's revealed, put its two matching Finale Rules cards side by side, coloured

121
00:06:45,839 --> 00:06:50,051
diamonds lined up, and follow them. For example, Luxuriant Growth pairs with The

122
00:06:50,051 --> 00:06:52,209
Greenhouse and uses the Greenhouse token.

123
00:06:52,209 --> 00:06:54,684
The Finale card's back shows the Minion Action.

124
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:59,538
Before the Finale, you win if there are no Plants, Pods or Assimilated on the board

125
00:06:59,538 --> 00:07:01,047
at the end of the Killer phase.

126
00:07:01,267 --> 00:07:05,211
After the Finale is revealed, its Finale Rules cards give you different win

127
00:07:05,211 --> 00:07:05,789
conditions.

128
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:10,417
You lose the usual way, or instantly if Evolution finds you in a space with a Pod

129
00:07:10,417 --> 00:07:14,607
and no Victims, or if a Victim must be assimilated and every token is in use.

130
00:07:15,433 --> 00:07:18,237
A few tips. Destroy Plants before they turn into Pods;

131
00:07:18,237 --> 00:07:20,105
one health each, so any hit will do.

132
00:07:20,325 --> 00:07:24,798
Keep Victims out of spaces with Podarch tokens, and never end a turn alone with a

133
00:07:24,798 --> 00:07:25,019
Pod.

134
00:07:25,239 --> 00:07:29,524
Killing Assimilated raises Bloodlust and turns them Hostile sooner, so choose those

135
00:07:29,524 --> 00:07:30,401
fights carefully.

136
00:07:30,621 --> 00:07:34,260
Players win about fifty eight per cent of logged games against the Podarchs.

137
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:34,739
Good luck.

